cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RPP, please cite it as below."
title: "RPP: Rover Photogrammetry Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  RPP (Rover Photogrammetry Pipeline) is a Python package that turns Mars rover images from NASA's Planetary Data
  System (PDS) into aligned, true-scale 3D models with structure from motion, combining images from many rover stops.
  It fetches PDS products from the Mars 2020 Perseverance Navcam, Hazcam and Mastcam-Z cameras (Curiosity support is
  experimental), converts their color, masks rover hardware and shadows with a fine-tuned convolutional network, and
  translates the mission's CAHV, CAHVOR and CAHVORE camera models or applies versioned in-flight models that vary
  with temperature, focus, zoom and sol. Each stop is placed from the rover's localization, and the images are
  aligned with COLMAP feature matching and RPP's own weighted bundle adjustment with telemetry priors and stereo
  rigs. Results open in COLMAP, Agisoft Metashape and Nerfstudio. Experimental station products (meshes, depth and
  normal maps, and omnidirectional stereo panoramas) feed the Rover Photogrammetry Viewer (RPV) for web browsers, VR
  headsets and smartphones.
